  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145372",
      "title": "What Is \"File-based Routing\"? And Why Is It Helpful?",
      "lectureOrder": 230,
      "videoOrder": 214,
      "sourceHash": "4e15cf3cc78a998909ed56e774c7bbd55606b88407385dc128cbec0969607b61",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "In traditional React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 9.67,
          "en": "so in a React apps where you are not using Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.67,
          "end": 12.61,
          "en": "you set up routing like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.61,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "You have some code in one of your React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 20.82,
          "en": "where you do add various route related components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "from react-router-dom, which is a great library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 28.41,
          "en": "And there of course isn't necessarily anything wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 32.47,
          "en": "with this setup, but this is not how we'll do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.47,
          "end": 34.33,
          "en": "with Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.33,
          "end": 37.2,
          "en": "There, we don't install React router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 40.57,
          "en": "and we won't write any JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.57,
          "end": 43.4,
          "en": "or any JavaScript code at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.4,
          "end": 48.4,
          "en": "when it comes to defining our routes and our page structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.49,
          "end": 53.49,
          "en": "Instead with Next.js, we create React component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 57.05,
          "en": "So regular React component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.05,
          "end": 59.44,
          "en": "in a special folder, as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.44,
          "end": 64.08,
          "en": "and we will then let Next.js infer our routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 69.08,
          "en": "in our project from that folder structure we set up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.47,
          "end": 72.22,
          "en": "We use the special pages folder for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72.22,
          "end": 75.095,
          "en": "because Next.js will automatically look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.095,
          "end": 80.095,
          "en": "into that pages folder to infer our route structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 82.03999999999999,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "Now, how does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 86.12,
          "en": "Well, let's consider this example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 86.12,
          "end": 89.03999999999999,
          "en": "This example pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 91.15,
          "en": "Here in this pages folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.15,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "we would have an index.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 96.1,
          "en": "and then as a sibling to that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.1,
          "end": 98.50999999999999,
          "en": "we have the about.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.50999999999999,
          "end": 100.46000000000001,
          "en": "And then we have the products folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.46000000000001,
          "end": 103.84,
          "en": "as a sibling to the index and about JS files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.84,
          "end": 106.68,
          "en": "so as a sub folder in pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.68,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "and in products, we have two additional JavaScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 112.8,
          "en": "the index.js file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.8,
          "end": 115.53999999999999,
          "en": "but now in products instead of just pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.53999999999999,
          "end": 119.77000000000001,
          "en": "and then a file with a rather strange file name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.77000000000001,
          "end": 121.39,
          "en": "square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.39,
          "end": 125.723,
          "en": "and then id inside of those square brackets dot JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 129.61,
          "en": "Now we'll come back to this strange looking file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.61,
          "end": 130.98,
          "en": "in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.98,
          "end": 134.76,
          "en": "Let's first of all, have a look at what Next.js would do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.76,
          "end": 137.03,
          "en": "It would look at the pages folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.03,
          "end": 141.89,
          "en": "and now infer a couple of routes we wanna support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.89,
          "end": 144.5,
          "en": "For example, based on index.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.5,
          "end": 147.76,
          "en": "it would infer that this should be our main starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.76,
          "end": 152.62,
          "en": "for requests to our domain slash nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.62,
          "end": 154.463,
          "en": "So for an empty path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.32999999999998,
          "end": 159.1,
          "en": "For about.js, it would infer that we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.1,
          "end": 161.05,
          "en": "wanna load an about page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.05,
          "end": 165.28,
          "en": "so it would in the end just render the component returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.28,
          "end": 167.39,
          "en": "in the about.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.39,
          "end": 172.39,
          "en": "and it would load that component for our domain.com/about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.24,
          "end": 177.3,
          "en": "So it takes the file name as a path, as you can tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 182.27,
          "en": "with the exception of index.js, that's a special file name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.27,
          "end": 187.24,
          "en": "which will be assume as the route path for the given folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.24,
          "end": 188.073,
          "en": "in which you are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.073,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "So directly in the pages folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 192.78,
          "en": "index.js would be our route path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 195.32,
          "en": "and empty slash after the domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.32,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "Inside of products, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 202.22,
          "en": "index.js would be loaded from my domain.com/products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 205.37,
          "en": "So not slash products slash index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.37,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "but just slash products slash nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 212.35,
          "en": "loads index just as just my domain slash nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.35,
          "end": 215.06,
          "en": "loads index in the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.06,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "If we have a file named differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 219.23,
          "en": "like about.js here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.23,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "then this file name is used as a path segment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 226.64,
          "en": "And alternative to naming a file about.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.64,
          "end": 231.3,
          "en": "therefore, would also be to create a sub folder named about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.3,
          "end": 234.25,
          "en": "with an index.js file inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.25,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "that would lead to the same result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 240.62,
          "en": "because index.js files are treated in that special way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.62,
          "end": 241.82,
          "en": "I just explained.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.82,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "And of course, we're going to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 245.61,
          "en": "all of that in action soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 249.62,
          "en": "Now, what about this strange square bracket file name here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.62,
          "end": 254.62,
          "en": "This is a special notation we can use to add dynamic path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.9,
          "end": 258.61,
          "en": "So for example, if we have the product detail page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.61,
          "end": 261.93,
          "en": "so if we show some content for a selected product,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.93,
          "end": 264.5,
          "en": "then of course we wanna show that same page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.5,
          "end": 266.39,
          "en": "for different products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.39,
          "end": 269.98,
          "en": "So our URL would look something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.98,
          "end": 274.98,
          "en": "our domain.com/products/and then the ID of a given product.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.71,
          "end": 278.07,
          "en": "And of course we can have multiple products",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.07,
          "end": 279.90999999999997,
          "en": "and therefore multiple IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.90999999999997,
          "end": 282.33,
          "en": "And that's why this is dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.33,
          "end": 285.12,
          "en": "The ID isn't always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.12,
          "end": 286.63,
          "en": "And as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.63,
          "end": 290.38,
          "en": "we can't predefine our different detailed pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.38,
          "end": 292.04,
          "en": "for the different products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.04,
          "end": 295.15999999999997,
          "en": "because a, we might not know in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.15999999999997,
          "end": 297.06,
          "en": "how many products we'll have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 301.63,
          "en": "and b, even if we knew, it's always the same page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.63,
          "end": 304.79,
          "en": "Just the data on the page will be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.79,
          "end": 309.79,
          "en": "And that's why Next.js supports such dynamic paths as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 310.6,
          "end": 313.38,
          "en": "with that special file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.38,
          "end": 315.16,
          "en": "So that is the equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.16,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "to defining such a dynamic path with React router like this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
